                    {
                        "content": {
                            "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
                            "params": {
                                "text": "<h2 id=\"ch1-formulas\">Formulas</h2>\n<p>Inline written as dollars: \\(E = mc^2\\), which is the spelling Markdown editors know and the\none <code>H5P.MathDisplay</code> does not.</p>\n<p>Display written as dollars, which both sides read, so it comes back out exactly as written:</p>\n<p>$$\\int_0^1 x^2\\,dx = \\frac{1}{3}$$</p>\n<p>Spread over several lines, which is one paragraph and therefore one formula:</p>\n<p>$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na &amp;= b + c \\\\\nd &amp;= e - f\n\\end{aligned}\n$$</p>\n<p>Markdown must not touch what is inside: \\(x_1 * x_2\\) keeps its underscore and its star, and\n\\(p \\$ q\\) keeps its escaped dollar.</p>\n<p>The backslash spellings are deliberately <em>not</em> math, because no Markdown editor renders\nthem as math either: (a_1 + a_2) and [\\sum_{i=1}^{n} i] are ordinary escaped brackets\nand come out as the literal characters the author asked for, leaving <code>MathDisplay</code> nothing\nto convert.</p>\n"
                            },
                            "metadata": {
